[71.233478, "o", "README.markdown:2:[![Linux build](https://travis-ci.org/stp/stp.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.org/stp/stp)\r\nREADME.markdown:3:[![Windows build](https://ci.appveyor.com/api/projects/status/35983b7cnrg37whk?svg=true)](https://ci.appveyor.com/project/msoos/stp)\r\nREADME.markdown:6:[![Codacy Badge](https://api.codacy.com/project/badge/Grade/f043efa22ea64e9ba44fde0f3a4fb09f)](https://www.codacy.com/app/soos.mate/cryptominisat?utm_source=github.com&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=msoos/cryptominisat&amp;utm_campaign=Badge_Grade)\r\nREADME.markdown:18:## Build and install\r\nREADME.markdown:20:For a quick install:\r\nREADME.markdown:23:sudo apt-get install cmake bison flex libboost-all-dev python perl minisat\r\nREADME.markdown:26:mkdir build\r\nREADME.markdown:27:cd build\r\nREADME.markdown:28:cmake ..\r\nREADME.markdown:29:make\r\nREADME.markdown:30:sudo make install\r\nREADME.markdown:77:## Detailed Building and Installation\r\nREADME.markdown:79:STP is built with [CMake](https://cmake.org/), version 3.0.2 or newer. CMake is a\r\nREADME.markdown:80:meta build system that generates build files for other tools such as\r\nREADME.markdown:81:make(1), Visual Studio, Xcode, etc.\r\nREADME.markdown:87:- ``CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`` - The build type (e.g. Release)\r\nREADME.markdown:88:- ``CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX`` - The prefix for install (e.g. /usr/local )\r\nREADME.markdown:91:- ``ENABLE_PYTHON_INTERFACE`` - Enable building the Python interface\r\nREADME.markdown:92:- ``PYTHON_EXECUTABLE`` - Set python executable in case you have more than one python installed\r\nREADME.markdown:94:- ``STATICCOMPILE`` - Build static libraries and binaries instead of dynamic\r\nREADME.markdown:96:### Dependencies\r\nREADME.markdown:97:STP relies on : boost, flex, bison and minisat. You can install these by:\r\nREADME.markdown:100:$ sudo apt-get install cmake bison flex libboost-all-dev python perl minisat\r\nREADME.markdown:103:STP uses minisat as its SAT solver by default but it also supports other SAT solvers including CryptoMiniSat as an optional extra. If installed, it will be detected during the cmake and used:\r\nREADME.markdown:106:$ git clone https://github.com/msoos/cryptominisat\r\nREADME.markdown:107:$ cd cryptominisat\r\nREADME.markdown:108:$ mkdir build && cd build\r\nREADME.markdown:109:$ cmake ..\r\nREADME.markdown:110:$ make\r\nREADME.markdown:111:$ sudo make install\r\nREADME.markdown:115:### Building a static library and binary\r\nREADME.markdown:118:$ mkdir build && cd build\r\nREADME.markdown:119:$ cmake -DSTATICCOMPILE=ON ..\r\nREADME.markdown:120:$ make\r\nREADME.markdown:121:$ sudo make install\r\nREADME.markdown:125:### Configuration and build options\r\nREADME.markdown:127:To tweak the build configuration:\r\nREADME.markdown:129:* Run ``cmake-gui /path/to/stp/source/root`` instead of ``cmake``. This\r\nREADME.markdown:131:  variables and lets you pick the build system generator.\r\nREADME.markdown:133:* Run ``ccmake`` instead of ``cmake``. This provides an ncurses terminal\r\nREADME.markdown:136:* Pass ``-D<VARIABLE>=<VALUE>`` options to ``cmake`` (not very user friendly).\r\nREADME.markdown:140:You can also tweak configuration later by running `make edit_cache` and edit any configuration variables, reconfigure and then regenerate the build system. After configuration, build by running `make`.\r\nREADME.markdown:142:You can use the `-j<n>` flag to significantly to decrease build time by running `<n>` jobs in parallel (e.g. `make -j4`).\r\nREADME.markdown:149:pip install lit\r\nREADME.markdown:150:mkdir build\r\nREADME.markdown:151:cd build\r\nREADME.markdown:152:cmake -DENABLE_TESTING=ON ..\r\nREADME.markdown:153:make\r\nREADME.markdown:154:make check\r\nREADME.markdown:157:### Installing\r\nREADME.markdown:159:To install run `make install` and to uninstall run `make uninstall`. The root of installation is controlled by the `CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX` variable at configure time. You can change this by running `make edit_cache` and editing the value of `CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX`.\r\nREADME.markdown:162:### Building on Visual Studio\r\nREADME.markdown:165:git installed. Get zlib:\r\nREADME.markdown:172:mkdir build\r\nREADME.markdo"]
[71.233647, "o", "wn:173:mkdir myinstall\r\nREADME.markdown:174:cd build\r\nREA"]
[71.234078, "o", "DME.markdown:175:cmake -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=\"..\\myinstall\" ..\r\nREADME.markdown:176:cmake --build .\r\nREADME.markdown:177:cmake --build . --target install\r\nREADME.markdown:180:Get minisat:\r\nREADME.markdown:184:git clone https://github.com/stp/minisat\r\nREADME.markdown:185:cd minisat\r\nREADME.markdown:186:mkdir build\r\nREADME.markdown:187:mkdir myinstall\r\nREADME.markdown:188:cd build\r\nREADME.markdown:189:cmake -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=\"..\\myinstall\" -DZLIB_ROOT=\"..\\..\\zlib\\myinstall\" ..\r\nREADME.markdown:190:cmake --build .\r\nREADME.markdown:191:cmake --build . --target install\r\nREADME.markdown:201:Finally, Build STP:\r\nREADME.markdown:207:mkdir build\r\nREADME.markdown:208:cd build\r\nREADME.markdown:209:cmake -DBoost_USE_STATIC_LIBS=ON -DENABLE_TESTING=ON -DPYTHON_EXECUTABLE=\"C:\\Program Files\\Python36\\\\python.exe\" -DLIT_TOOL=\"C:\\Program Files\\Python36\\Scripts\\\\lit.exe\" -DMINISAT_LIBDIR=\"..\\..\\minisat\\myinstall\\lib\" -DMINISAT_INCLUDE_DIRS=\"..\\..\\minisat\\myinstall\\include\" -DZLIB_ROOT=\"..\\..\\zlib\\myinstall\" -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=\"C:\\cygwi"]
[71.23415, "o", "n64\" ..\r\nREADME.markdown:210:cmake --build .\r\nREADME.markdown:211:cmake --build . --target install\r\nREADME.markdown:214:### Building Docker\r\nREADME.markdown:219:docker build -t stp .\r\nCMakeLists.txt:22:cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.3 FATAL_ERROR)\r\nCMakeLists.txt:23:set(CMAKE_C_STANDARD 99)\r\nCMakeLists.txt:24:set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 11)\r\nCMakeLists.txt:27:include(GNUInstallDirs)\r\n"]
